  "preamble": "The shift from [p] to [v] is a hallmark of Western Romance lenition. It involves a two-stage process where the voiceless stop first voices to [b] and then spirantizes into a voiced fricative, typically in intervocalic positions.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Voicing, Spirantization, Lenition",
